WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.240
Part 1. You will hear a woman phoning to find out about one-day classes held at

00:00:07.240 --> 00:00:12.360
Stainford College. First, you have some time to look at

00:00:12.360 --> 00:00:15.880
questions 1 to 5.

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:45.000
Now listen carefully and answer questions 1 to 5.

00:00:45.000 --> 00:00:51.840
Hello, Stainford College External Course Registration. Can I help you?

00:00:51.840 --> 00:00:58.599
Yeah, I'm ringing to find out about one-day classes next year. I got a leaflet about them

00:00:58.599 --> 00:01:04.720
in the post, but I lost it. And I understand some of the classes are filling up fast,

00:01:04.720 --> 00:01:09.000
so I might need to book quite soon if I want to go ahead.

00:01:09.000 --> 00:01:13.080
Sure. Can you remember which one you were considering?

00:01:13.080 --> 00:01:18.480
There were a few, actually. I remember there was one on how to make Vietnamese food that

00:01:18.480 --> 00:01:24.279
sounded good. I think that was on the 13th of January. It cost about £60.

00:01:24.279 --> 00:01:32.480
Yes, you're right about the date, but it's £59, actually. It's a very popular class,

00:01:32.480 --> 00:01:38.199
and among other things, the teacher explains how Vietnamese food includes lots of different

00:01:38.199 --> 00:01:44.440
herbs. I'm afraid that all the places are taken at present, but I can put you on the

00:01:44.440 --> 00:01:46.559
waiting list if you want.

00:01:46.559 --> 00:01:52.839
No, that's OK. I'm quite interested in the bread-making class. That's in March

00:01:52.839 --> 00:01:54.800
some time, isn't it?

00:01:54.800 --> 00:01:59.400
Yeah, the 20th of March. Would you like to register for that?

00:01:59.400 --> 00:02:02.599
I'm not sure. How much is it?

00:02:02.599 --> 00:02:09.960
The actual cost is £48, but then there's an extra charge as well as that for the ingredients.

00:02:09.960 --> 00:02:15.199
I'm not sure how much that is. No more than £20, I think.

00:02:15.199 --> 00:02:18.399
So what sorts of things do they make in the class?

00:02:18.440 --> 00:02:25.160
Oh, various types of bread. I think they make white bread and then they make sourdough.

00:02:25.160 --> 00:02:30.600
That seems to be very fashionable at present. And they learn how to make pizza, which is

00:02:30.600 --> 00:02:32.080
apparently really good.

00:02:32.080 --> 00:02:38.160
Well, I'd definitely be interested in that. But there were also a few other classes that

00:02:38.160 --> 00:02:43.520
sounded interesting. I think there was one on face massage. I'd love to learn how to

00:02:43.520 --> 00:02:44.520
do that.

00:02:44.839 --> 00:02:52.399
Yeah, that's on the 23rd of February, and it costs just £35 for the day. The teacher's

00:02:52.399 --> 00:03:00.039
great. The type of massage done is a traditional technique used in India, and she actually

00:03:00.039 --> 00:03:07.800
did her training there. The massage is meant to relax you and get rid of lines and wrinkles.

00:03:07.800 --> 00:03:13.279
You practice it on yourself, so you have to take a mirror to the class so you can see

00:03:13.279 --> 00:03:14.279
what you're doing.

00:03:14.279 --> 00:03:15.279
OK.

00:03:18.800 --> 00:03:25.600
Before you hear the rest of the conversation, you have some time to look at questions 6-10.

00:03:43.279 --> 00:03:55.279
Now listen, and answer questions 6-10.

00:03:55.279 --> 00:04:01.279
And I think there was a class in candle making?

00:04:01.279 --> 00:04:09.679
Yes, that's sometime in April, I think. Let me check. Er, yes, it's on the 6th. It was

00:04:09.679 --> 00:04:18.000
on the 23rd of January, but they had to change the date. It's just £52. That's a popular

00:04:18.000 --> 00:04:24.640
course too. I think one reason why people like it is because the candles are all made

00:04:24.640 --> 00:04:31.040
out of natural products. It's filling up fast, but there's still a few places left.

00:04:31.040 --> 00:04:37.640
Yes, one of my friends did that class. She said the candles make really good presents.

00:04:37.640 --> 00:04:39.640
In fact, she gave me one.

00:04:39.640 --> 00:04:45.640
Ah, by the way, have you heard about the class on silk painting? That's being held on the

00:04:45.640 --> 00:04:52.959
18th of May. You learn how to create designs on silk fabric and colour them using special

00:04:52.959 --> 00:05:00.440
dyes. Apparently, people can produce beautiful artworks that way, either to put on the wall

00:05:00.440 --> 00:05:09.239
as a picture, or to use for something like a scarf. It's £67.50, which is really good

00:05:09.239 --> 00:05:15.399
value I think. There's a similar class I've seen that was £110.

00:05:15.399 --> 00:05:19.200
That sounds interesting. Would I need to bring the silk?

00:05:19.200 --> 00:05:25.359
No, the only thing is everyone has to bring something to protect their clothing, like

00:05:25.359 --> 00:05:31.559
an apron if you've got one, or a shirt that you don't use anymore because the dye can

00:05:31.559 --> 00:05:33.559
really stain your clothes.

00:05:33.559 --> 00:05:41.359
Right. Then the last class I was considering was a bit different. That was on DIY for beginners.

00:05:41.359 --> 00:05:47.359
I'd like to learn how to do household repairs. Are there any places left on that?

00:05:47.359 --> 00:05:55.359
That's on the 24th of February. Yes, there are a few places. It's a bit more expensive.

00:05:55.359 --> 00:06:04.359
It's £125, but it's a very popular class. You learn how to use an electric drill and a saw.

00:06:04.359 --> 00:06:10.359
Yeah, that would be really useful. And I even need to learn how to use a hammer because

00:06:10.359 --> 00:06:12.359
I always end up hitting my fingers.

00:06:12.359 --> 00:06:20.359
Yes, you'll do that too. And when you've learned how to use the basic tools, you do a practical job,

00:06:20.359 --> 00:06:23.359
which is fixing a shelf to a wall.

00:06:23.359 --> 00:06:30.359
Great, just what I need to know. Right, well, I'd like to enrol for that and also for the...

00:06:33.359 --> 00:06:39.359
That is the end of part one. You now have one minute to check your answers to part one.

